      <title>A White House meeting, a tanker off Qatar, and drones over Ryazan</title>
      <description>Melania Trump hosts Russian and Ukrainian envoys as talks open in Brussels and the Komyshuvakha toll rises to forty, mediators push a blockade-for-Hormuz framework after a tanker is hit north of Qatar, Ukraine hits Ryazan and an Ozon warehouse, and the Theodore Roosevelt heads west.&lt;p&gt;Sources:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/nov/5/melania-trump-hosts-rare-ukraine-russia-meeting-white-house/"&gt;Washington Times: Melania Trump hosts envoys&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.nbcnews.com/world/ukraine/melania-trump-host-russia-ukraine-representatives-white-house-rare-mee-rcna607390"&gt;NBC News: White House meeting&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.washingtontimes.com/news/2026/nov/5/russia-ukraine-trade-missile-drone-strikes-technical-talks-begin/"&gt;Washington Times: Brussels talks and overnight strikes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.intellinews.com/missile-war-monitor-more-than-200-drones-attack-russia-s-ryazan-region-as-komyshuvakha-toll-rises-to-40-482173/"&gt;bne IntelliNews: Ryazan and Komyshuvakha toll&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/11/05/ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-ryazan-region-with-fires-reported-at-oil-refinery-and-wildberries-warehouse"&gt;Meduza: Ryazan strikes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kyivpost.com/post/89205"&gt;Kyiv Post: 128 drones and two missiles&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://odessa-journal.com/ukrainian-drones-strike-major-ozon-warehouse-in-russia"&gt;Odessa Journal: Ozon warehouse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.ukrinform.net/rubric-ato/4181554-war-update-179-clashes-on-front-line-fiercest-fighting-in-pokrovsk-sector.html"&gt;Ukrinform: front-line update&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.dawn.com/news/2042327/tanker-struck-by-2-unidentified-projectiles-north-of-qatar-crew-stat